-- title:
--   Transition morphisms pull each Mumford chart back to its counterpart
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$ and a domain $\mathcal O$ that is a discrete valuation ring, with an irreducible element $\pi$ whose residue ring $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements, together with a fraction field $K_0$ of $\mathcal O$ and the element $g_1 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ whose matrix is $\operatorname{diag}(\pi,1)$; let $N$ be a subgroup of $\mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ and $n$ a natural number. Let $L$ and $L'$ be Mumford gluing data of level $n$ and $n+1$ for these parameters: each consists of a scheme $Z$, flat and separated over $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O/(\pi^{n+1}))$ (resp. $(\pi^{n+2})$), a family of open immersions $\zeta_h$ from the spectrum of the edge chart ring modulo $\pi^{n+1}$ (resp. $\pi^{n+2}$) indexed by $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$, which lie over the base, cover $Z$ by finitely many members and are invariant under left multiplication by elements of $N$, together with the localisation map $\iota$ to the vertex chart ring and the automorphisms $\tau$ with their compatibilities; here the edge chart ring $\mathtt{chartERing}\ \mathcal O\ \pi\ r$ is the localisation of $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}(\mathrm{Fin}\ 2,\mathcal O)$ modulo the principal ideal generated by $\mathtt{edgeRel}\ \mathcal O\ \pi$, away from the image of $\mathtt{edgeDiscr}\ \mathcal O\ r$. Assume given a morphism $z_t : L.Z \to L'.Z$ such that for every $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ the composite $L.\zeta_h$ followed by $z_t$ equals the closed immersion $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the reduction map $A/(\pi^{n+2}) \to A/(\pi^{n+1})$ followed by $L'.\zeta_h$. Then for every $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ the preimage under $z_t$ of the open subset $\operatorname{im} L'.\zeta_h$ of $L'.Z$ is exactly the open subset $\operatorname{im} L.\zeta_h$ of $L.Z$.
--
--   This is the chartwise compatibility step in Mumford's formal gluing construction of the Čerednik–Drinfel'd formal upper half plane: a transition morphism between consecutive levels that respects the indexing of the charts cannot enlarge the chart with index $h$. It is used in the proof that the level-$(n+1)$ datum restricts over $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O/(\pi^{n+1}))$ to the level-$n$ datum, i.e. in [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.MumfordGlueLevel.isPullback_zb_of_forall_zeta_comp_eq`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.MumfordGlueLevel.isPullback_zb_of_forall_zeta_comp_eq).
